rong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"40dc2e052b690b02\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"530c2b19ce4fd12b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"530c2b19ce4fd12b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cf8b8538db77dadc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUse the drop-down menu to select a state/jurisdiction and click on a student group thumbnail to see average mathematics scores for fourth-grade public school students over time in the selected state/jurisdiction. ... Use the drop-down menus to select a state/jurisdiction and a student group to view changes in the percentage distribution for that group over time. Read about changes in NAEP&#x27;s reporting for racial/ethnic groups.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cf8b8538db77dadc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b084f972cb6baeeb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b084f972cb6baeeb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83762edaf64b9a30\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics a