{"type": "message", "id": "89e63e6a", "parentId": "f1d364a9", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T19:18:20.617Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_4207cdec64ca40c1a4b25e57", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 grade 8 math \\\"average score\\\" state Kentucky 270 Kansas Arizona \\\"South Carolina\\\" site:nces.ed.gov OR site:nationsreportcard.gov\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 865,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71e53ff4bbc6e199\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71e53ff4bbc6e199\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"29f68015afb49060\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from <strong>2 to 14 points</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"29f68015afb49060\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"69dbde976bcd02e2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"69dbde976bcd02e2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"90d98a2557d6a5ef\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics ... compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"90d98a2557d6a5ef\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d58e4024e53dd495\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d58e4024e53dd495\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b6764a04ae34c967\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b6764a04ae34c967\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6158c1e0d4c25309\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6158c1e0d4c25309\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b9617e03315e9a6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b9617e03315e9a6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"048438bef3054987\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: District Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"048438bef3054987\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/districts/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7c8745180bc2f237\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOf the 23 TUDA districts that scored lower in 2022 compared to 2019, nine districts scored lower than the large city average score, 4 districts had an average score that was higher than the large city average score, and 10 districts had an average score that was not significantly different from the large city average score.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7c8745180bc2f237\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math \"average score\" state Kentucky 270 Kansas Arizona \"South Carolina\" site:nces.ed.gov OR site:nationsreportcard.gov", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 865, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71e53ff4bbc6e199\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71e53ff4bbc6e199\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"29f68015afb49060\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from <strong>2 to 14 points</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"29f68015afb49060\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"69dbde976bcd02e2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"69dbde976bcd02e2\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"90d98a2557d6a5ef\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics ... compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"90d98a2557d6a5ef\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d58e4024e53dd495\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d58e4024e53dd495\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b6764a04ae34c967\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b6764a04ae34c967\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6158c1e0d4c25309\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6158c1e0d4c25309\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b9617e03315e9a6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b9617e03315e9a6\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"048438bef3054987\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: District Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"048438bef3054987\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/districts/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c8745180bc2f237\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOf the 23 TUDA districts that scored lower in 2022 compared to 2019, nine districts scored lower than the large city average score, 4 districts had an average score that was higher than the large city average score, and 10 districts had an average score that was not significantly different from the large city average score.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c8745180bc2f237\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775589500615}}
